===Mastery Strategies===
{{MastComp|{{MastStrat|first|Active|+60}}|{{MastStrat|second and sixth|Collect and use|Use}}|{{MastStrat|third|Meters|3Star|Note that teleporting will count as moving, so try inviting a Toon to finish faster.}}|{{MastStrat|fourth|Machine}}|{{MastStrat|fifth|Reach/do floors}}}}
==Requirement Strategies==
*For the first requirement, focus on picking up [[Research Capsules]] and extracting [[Machines]]. The Machine and Capsule count increases the further you descend, so you can earn more {{II|Ichor|name=true}}.
*For the second requirement, you can walk near {{CI|Twisted Glisten|name=true}} while he is in his Passive state to obtain Research. Playing as {{CI|Rodger|name=true}} also helps getting it faster because of his Passive [[Ability]]. This will be easier if Twisted Glisten is on the [[Daily Twisted Board]].
*For the third requirement, you can go into multiple runs and do as many machines as you can. To do this, focus on using a Toon that has a fast Extraction Speed or Big Skill Check, you can also use [[Trinkets]] that increase your Skill Check or Extraction.

==Strategies==
Glisten has the highest [[Extraction Speed]] in the game, making him one of the best extractor [[Toons]]. While Glisten's small [[Skill Check]] may make the rest superior strictly in terms of extracting, Glisten's average [[Movement Speed]], [[Stamina]], and easy getaway [[Ability]] make him arguably a better [[Toon]]. However, both his lackluster Skill Check and shared low [[Stealth]] can become issues. 

Glisten's Active Ability, {{AI|Glisten|name=true}}, allows him to easily get away from [[Twisteds]] that are chasing you, out of dead ends, or to cover ground quickly. Line of Sight isn't required to use this Ability, so it makes it even easier. However, watching your Active Ability's cooldown is necessary, as using it at the wrong time can make you unable to escape tricky situations later. For example, if you're on the [[Library Floor]] and you were to do the last [[Machine]] in a room adjacent to the [[Elevator]], you can teleport through the walls and save a lot of Stamina. However, there is a risk that the target Toon that you teleport to has a Twisted chasing them or near them, which could attract the Twisted's attention to you instead. You should also note Glisten doesn't have an extremely long range for his Ability. It's also worth noting that, when Glisten is afflicted with the -75% Extraction Speed [[Debuff]] from using his ability, he is left with 0.375 Extraction Speed for 10 seconds (passively filling only 3.75 units compared to his usual 15 units in that time).

Conversely, you may also use this Ability to ''attract'' Twisteds' attention. His low Stealth and average Speed/Stamina make it possible to use Reflection to save teammates, though caution must be taken. Using Glisten's ability can be disorienting, so really try to think through any complicated maneuvers you try to pull off.

Some ideas for the usage of Glisten's Ability could be:
*Skipping long hallways/staircases;
*Accessing [[Items]] or [[Machines]] more quickly;
*Making it to the [[Elevator]] faster during [[Panic Mode]];
*Avoiding stealing aggro from Distractors or easily passing Twisteds off to them;
*Saving higher-stealth/lower-speed teammates;
*Escaping {{CI|Twisted Razzle & Dazzle|name=true}} or {{CI|Twisted Rodger|name=true}} if a teammate activates them;
*Passing through {{CI|Twisted Blot|name=true}}'s hands (not recommended);
*Getting out of dead ends;
*Baiting {{CI|Twisted Vee|name=true}}/ranged Twisteds to give Distractors a head-start;
*Luring Twisteds away from the Elevator during Panic Mode and teleporting back in order to give teammates better chances of making it;
*Spending more time collecting Items or completing objectives by using your Ability as a fail-safe on large maps;
*Teleporting to a Toon working on a Duo Machine with an empty slot.

Take note that Glisten's Ability can be difficult to aim and may put you directly into danger if used on the wrong person—try to get used to using it on the correct teammate before using it in high-pressure situations. In addition, Twisteds do not immediately forget your position after you teleport; their normal attention span still applies and they will continue to head towards you if they do not spot a different teammate, so try to teleport to a Toon far enough or is blocked by walls for effective escape.

It's best to have distractors like {{CI|Eclipse|name=true}}, {{CI|Goob|name=true}}, or {{CI|Looey|name=true}} to make sure that Twisteds don't bother Glisten while he's extracting, since they have the same, if not lower Stealth as him. However, other distractors can work, as long as you are out of the way. Watching Glisten's Stealth Stat and distance to the Twisteds is necessary because of this.

Glisten most benefits from Items that are centered towards extraction like {{II|Instructions|name=false}} and {{II|Jumper Cable|name=false|plural=a}}. He can also make use of mobility Items such as {{II|Speed Candy|name=false|plural=a}} as backups when his Ability is on cooldown, or no Toons are in range for him to teleport.

Overall, Glisten is a pretty great extractor, although his Skill Check and Stealth require some patience. He has an edge when it comes to survival thanks to his Ability, but note the cooldown and range. He struggles a bit in solo runs since his Ability is completely unusable, so he may not be the best choice for such a run.

