==Trivia==
*Despite popular belief due to his flamboyant personality, Glisten is not canonically homosexual, as confirmed by [[Qwelver]].<ref>https://discord.com/channels/969934252844138496/1251545388259741768/1280670014147530773</ref>
*Glisten was originally a [[w:c:donthugme|Don't Hug Me I'm Scared]] OC that [[Qwelver]] made.
*Glisten is the second non-{{Type|Main}} [[Toon]] to have 5{{Star}} on a [[Stat]].
*Glisten owns a wired microphone. He is shown holding it in his info card artwork and mentions it breaking to [[Vee]] in one of their dialogues.
*Glisten and [[Scraps]] have a similar Active [[Ability]], going to a [[Toon]]'s location quickly, with the differences being that Scraps' Ability needs direct line of sight to use and works on [[Machines]], while Glisten's doesn't and has a cooldown 4 times longer.
*His name, Glisten, means "to reflect a sparkling light or a faint intermittent glow", reflecting his status as a mirror.
**Before that, he was originally going to be called "Mirror"<ref>https://discord.com/channels/969934252844138496/1251545388259741768/1261326631029444689</ref>, with the name change being quite obvious: Mirror would be quite a boring name.
*Glisten is designation ''SC-007'' with the '''SC''' standing for Side Character.
*Glisten receives the {{Debuff|Confused|III}} [[Debuff]] upon using his Active [[Ability]].
**According to a note from the [[Roleplaying Mode]], Glisten gets the Debuff from using his Active Ability because it disorients him and makes him feel dizzy, causing him to bump into things. Glisten's dialogue with {{CI|Rodger|name=true}} and gossip from {{CI|Dyle|name=true}} confirms this.
***This could also be a potential reason on top of his insecurities on why he is so concerned about his appearance and often asks other [[Toons]] if he looks good in his dialogues like {{CI|Sprout|name=true}}'s or {{CI|Boxten|name=true}}'s.
**This makes him the first Toon to obtain a visible Debuff from an Ability.
*Glisten's bedroom shares a floor with [[Boxten]], {{CI|Brightney|name=true}}, {{CI|Goob|name=true}}, {{CI|Poppy|name=true}}, {{CI|Razzle & Dazzle|name=true}}, [[Scraps]], and {{CI|Shrimpo|name=true}} in [[Roleplay Mode]].
**Glisten is the only post [[Changelog|v0.1]] [[Toon]] to have a Roleplay room.
*Glisten's insecurity about himself and obsession with appearing perfect to the others may tie in to his {{CI|Twisted Glisten}}[[Twisted Glisten|Twisted counterpart]]'s autophobia (fear of being abandoned and/or all alone).
**Notes that can be found in Glisten's Room in the [[Roleplaying Mode]] hints at this, both of which involve him overworking himself in some way.
***In one of the notes, Glisten mentions that he repeatedly practices his mirror trick to the point of becoming dizzy. He admits that he hides that fact from the others, as he doesn't want them to think he can't "handle everything."
***Another letter has scribbled text that says, "I just wish everyone could see that (I'm there at the best times)", implying that Glisten believes his efforts are still not good enough for the other [[Toons]].
**As Twisted Glisten, he's the most insecure in this state and desperate for company. The majority of his dialogue usually consists of a plea for companionship or anguish of being left all alone once his loneliness meter maxes out.
**In his conversation with {{CI|Toodles|name=true}}, he is shown getting defensive when Toodles mentions him crying and complaining to [[Rodger]], this could indicate Glisten has told him of his insecurities, or at least some parts of it.
*Glisten is implied to be friends with [[Razzle & Dazzle]], as shown in their Dialogue.
**This is further explained by one of his letters, stating 'I guess Razzle & Dazzle are fine.'
*Glisten seems to dislike {{CI|Finn|name=true}} and his puns, based on their interaction and one of Glisten's notes in his room saying, "I'm just happy it isn't Finn!"
*There is a glitch that if two or more Glistens teleport to each other, all the Confused III effects can be given to one of the Glistens stacking the effect, causing a major amount of [[Debuffs]].
*In a Discord Poll, it was decided that Glisten has a better side Profile than [[Rodger]].
*Glisten shares many similarities with [[Vee]].
**Both have a bow (Vee on her neck and Glisten on his waist), similar facial expressions (that also resemble their similar personalities), both cross their arms in their idle poses, same Extraction Speed, Stealth and Stamina (5 Stars, 2 Stars and 3 Stars respectively), and both owning a microphone (Glisten's microphone is seen in his Introduction Card and mentioned in his dialogue with Vee).
***This reflects how Glisten sees Vee as an inspiration to him.<ref>https://discord.com/channels/969934252844138496/969934252844138499/1372557120393842759</ref>
****Glisten also has Vee's "Smile" poster in his room.
*****Also, as seen in the video "[https://www.youtube.com/shorts/eJPtxkaDI7I Don't forget to recharge!]", Glisten is very worried when he sees Vee on the ground, probably because Vee is his inspiration and he doesn't want to lose her.
******If you look closely in the part where Glisten cries when trying to wake Vee, Glisten can be seen crying small amounts of [[Ichor]].
*Glisten harbors a dislike for clowns and likely {{CI|Looey|name=true}}'s Circus Troupe by extension, based off his dialogue with [[Yatta]] and Looey.
*Glisten often uses laughter as a means of covering up his stress and insecurity as seen in many of his dialogues, specifically with {{CI|Astro|name=true}}, [[Brightney]], {{CI|Cosmo|name=true}}, {{CI|Rudie|name=true}}, {{CI|Tisha|name=true}}, and [[Toodles]] and in one of his solo dialogues in the [[elevator]], making him somewhat similar to Looey (who serves as an example of being a performer who entertains others to cloak his sorrow).
**His more self-centered comments often also appear in similar scenarios, especially when [[Toons]] are checking in on him (e.g. [[Rodger]] and [[Sprout]]) when he gets something wrong such as in his dialogue with Cosmo or when Toons are teasing/insulting him such as [[Scraps]] and [[Vee]].
*Up until [[Changelog|v0.9.1]], Glisten was the most expensive non-{{Type|Main}} [[Toon]] in the game before getting replaced by [[Blot]].
*Glisten was the first [[Toon]] to have 2 idle animations, him checking his hand and his bow wiggling. The second being [[Yatta]], the third being {{CI|Bassie|name=true}}, the fourth being [[Blot]] and the fifth being [[Razzle & Dazzle]].
**After his optimization in [[Changelog|v0.12.1]], his two idle animations were combined to make one. As such, [[Yatta]] is now the first Toon to have 2 idle animations currently.
**He is the first one to not have optimizations upon his release, the other being Razzle & Dazzle.
***However, Razzle & Dazzle received the 2 idles after their optimizations, so Glisten was the only non-optimized Toon to have 2 idle animations.
*After [[Changelog|v0.10.1]], the "[[Astro]] in Stage Fright" poster is removed from Glisten's room, being replaced by the "SMILE!" poster instead.
*Glisten is the first {{Type|Rare}} [[Toon]] to get his optimizations post-release.
**He is also the only non-{{Type|Main}} to receive an optimization in [[Changelog|v0.12.1]].
**He is the only Rare Toon to not be optimized in pairs.
*Glisten is the first base game [[Toon]] to receive more than one Holiday [[Skin]] in a singular [[Event]], being Crimson Imp and Wrapped Chic in the [[2025 Halloween Event]]. The second ones are [[Rodger]] and [[Toodles]].
*Using Glisten's [[Ability]] to teleport to a [[Toon]] on the opposite side of an Ichor puddle will still give the {{Debuff|Illness|III}} [[Debuff]].
*Glisten is one of the few [[Toons]] where their [[Stats]] may be an all-round reflection of their character. In this case, Glisten has a strong desire to be perfect, thus his [[Extraction Speed]] is 5 Stars, possibly wanting to complete the Machines quickly to impress the other Toons. This is at the cost of harder [[Skill Check]]s, which may reflect the finer details and smaller room for mistakes involved with attempted perfection. He is a mirror, which are known to be very reflective of light, as represented with his 2 Star [[Stealth]].
*Glisten may have vision problems or a deficit in spatial awareness, based on his tendency to bump into walls or objects.
**The first point is also possibly referenced in the fact he didn't know that [[Cosmo]] has star freckles in all of the posters around [[Gardenview]], assuming he was wearing makeup instead. However, he could've simply never really noticed or didn't pay much attention.

